pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% Positive-direction companion of
% `incorrect/conclusion_BOUNDS_solx_unpreserved_objective`, and the completeness
% side of that fix: when the objective ranges only over preserved variables the
% class `solx` excludes is pinned down by the logged solution, so its minimum is
% exactly the representative's value and the new guard takes nothing away. The
% exact optimum 1 is still concluded after excluding an optimal solution.
f 1;
solx x1 ~x2;
output NONE;
conclusion BOUNDS 1 1 : x1 ~x2;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
